# Line-ending policy for the whole repository.
#
# Without this file git falls back to core.autocrlf, which is a per-developer
# setting. With core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) the index
# stays LF while the working tree becomes CRLF, and three things break on
# Windows checkouts only — CI never sees any of them:
#
#   * vitest cannot load a module whose shebang line ends CRLF. It fails with
#     a bare "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" because Vite's shebang
#     stripper leaves the \r behind. This took out both scripts/*.test.mjs
#     suites while `node --check` on the same files passed.
#   * `npm run format:check` reported 244 frontend files, every one of them
#     line-endings-only — .prettierrc pins endOfLine: lf.
#   * shell entrypoints must retain LF shebangs when they are executed in CI.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than a bare `text=auto` is the operative part: text=auto
# normalizes what git stores, eol=lf also dictates what git checks out. It is
# what makes the host platform stop mattering. .editorconfig already declares
# end_of_line = lf; this is the layer that enforces it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells need CRLF in batch files. None exist today — this keeps a
# future one from being silently broken by the rule above.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: no line-ending conversion and no attempted textual diff.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
